This would be an android app that scans a user's Google contacts and finds contacts with a birthday date as part of the contact info.  The app scans the contact periodically and creates a list of users and their birthdays.  At 9am (or a configurable time) on the day of their birthday, the phone will automatically send a text message to that contact wishing them a happy birthday.  The contact has to have a mobile number and a birthday as part of the contact profile and the app will allow for turning on/off the birthday sending per user with a simple switch.  It should be a simple, one-page app with a configurable time and configurable message.  The list of people and a checkbox to send or not send.  Simple, right?  The list and checkbox states are persistant, and maybe an optional "rescan" button.  That should be it.  Oh, and it has to wake up at the right time and auto-send the messages too.  If there are multiple people that have birthdays on the same day, then it should do all of those people, not just one.  Trying to make this as simple as possible.  The android build tools are installed on this machine. Kotlin is fine.
